{
  "description": "New pins of the relay, announced with a pins message on a control connection (RELAY-v0.md sections 4.1, 4.7 and 6.8). Each case: the pins the gateway has stored (active and backup, SHA-256 digests in canonical base64url), the pin of the connection, which is one of them and whose kind (active or backup) is the kind it had at the handshake, and the sets the relay announces in turn on this connection. Each step: the announced sets, whether the gateway answers stored or ignored, the pins stored afterwards, and whether the gateway closes this connection: it does as soon as a set is stored after which the pin of the connection is no longer stored at all (in either kind), after the answer if the set arrived on this connection, and also when the set arrived on another control connection. A step with arrived_on other is a set that another control connection of the gateway stored (the rules of Section 6.8 allowed it, so its answer is stored): expected is stored, stored_after is the result, and connection is the state of this connection afterwards. No step follows a step after which the connection is closed. The sets are written in any order; they are compared as sets. A set that is not stored changes nothing. The pins are the SHA-256 digests of the strings pin-A to pin-P; in the why texts they are the letters A to P. Durable storage and the answer within one heartbeat interval are not part of the cases.",
